<BaseLayout title="About">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>I'm Joe Caterine, the web and content strategist at the Virginia Institute of Marine Science, part of the College of William & Mary. I manage <a href="https://www.vims.edu">vims.edu</a> on Cascade CMS, where I've rolled out a web governance structure supporting 30 content editors, coordinated a content cleanup that removed over 20,000 outdated assets, and led the remediation of web accessibility issues ahead of the April 2026 WCAG 2.1 compliance deadline. I post about my latest VIMS web projects on <a href ="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jwcaterine/">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
    Before VIMS, I was the Digital Experience Manager at Virginia Sea Grant, where I led the development of the <a href="https://aquainfoexchange.org">Aquaculture Information Exchange</a> — a NOAA/USDA-backed platform for the American aquaculture community that grew from 200 to 2,000+ members under my watch.
    </p>

    <p>
    My interest in web development and programming started when I was a journalist. For a <a href="https://virginiamercury.com/2023/06/26/more-patients-in-crisis-falling-through-cracks-of-state-psychiatric-commitment-system/">story in the Virginia Mercury</a>, I analzyed data from the Department of Behavioral Health and Developmental Services to plot a rise in mental health crisis events. I also published a <a href="https://youtu.be/x9IDL8eruAw?si=eNvPyfSwFWVYBjPP">walkthrough on YouTube</a> explaing how I used PDFplumber to extract the data.
    </p>
    <p>
    In my spare time, I build small digital tools, like a CLI journaling system and a simple mobile-first PWA workout tracker. I am interested in helping to create digital tools that serve the people using them rather than extracting rent or attention from them. I think the ability to build, modify, and understand the digital tools that shape our daily lives is currently concentrated in too few hands. If you agree, let's talk!
    </p>
    <p>
    I live in coastal Virginia. You can find me on <a href="https://github.com/gam32bit">[GitHub]</a>, <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/jwcat757.bsky.social">[Bluesky]</a>, [LinkedIn], and [YouTube], or reach me at [email].
    </p>
</BaseLayout>
